{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h56d7o3yjo2ch5ifouj23itpdkxje4ihnpz72aiwjxab6ccunwwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Phase A — surface map** (all derived mechanically from the C source):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — the C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `process_decisions` (every other function in `lib.c` is `static`). Symbol diff C→Rust is **empty** in both debug and release. No C file was skipped: `c_src/src/` holds only `lib.c` and `main.c`, both translated.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 26 rows, one per distinct rejection (every `return -N`, every guard, every min/max constant, plus the `atoi`/`fgets` failure paths). No `assert`/`abort`/`return NULL` exists in the C.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 45 rows across `operation` × `param` × length tiers × content shapes × entry point.\n\n**Feature combinations:** `Cargo.toml` had no `[features]` and the C has no `#ifdef`/`option()`, so there are exactly two configurations (`--no-default-features` and default). `check_features.sh` enumerates them mechanically and runs check + build + test for each. All 77 tests pass in both, and in the release profile.\n\n**Two real divergences found and fixed** (both in the Rust; the C was never touched):\n\n1. **`validate_sequence` didn't mutate the caller's buffer.** The C does `bool *bools = (bool*)sequence;` and overwrites every byte in `[0, len)` with `0`/`1` — invisible from `main`, but fully observable by any FFI caller, and it happens even on the `-10`/`-11`/`-12` early returns. The translation had used a private `Vec<bool>`. Now reproduced byte-for-byte; `assert_same` compares the whole post-call buffer plus 16 guard bytes on *every* call.\n\n2. **`SIGPIPE` disposition + panicking stderr writes.** With stdout on a broken pipe the C dies with signal 13 while Rust exited **0**; with stderr on a broken pipe Rust exited **101** because `eprint!` panics where `fprintf` ignores failure. Fixed by restoring `SIG_DFL` for `SIGPIPE` at the top of `main` (via a direct `extern \"C\" { fn signal }` — no new dependency) and a non-panicking `write_stderr`.\n\nI also confirmed the harness has teeth: two deliberate negative-control mutations (an off-by-one, and reverting the buffer rewrite) each made 10–25 tests fail with precise diagnostics.\n\n**Structural additions:** a `cdylib` lib target + `#[no_mangle]` wrapper (`src/lib.rs`) whose access-window computation avoids forming a `length`-sized slice — needed because the C legitimately accepts `length == usize::MAX` with a 3-byte buffer for ops 0/1; `libloading` dev-dependency; `build_c_so.sh`, `check_features.sh`, `verify_all.sh`. Nothing under `c_src/` was modified (only the `c_src/build/` cmake dir the task asked for).\n\nTwo notes worth flagging, both **preserved** rather than \"fixed\": `validate_sequence`'s `return 40` and `apply_permissions`' trailing `return 0` are provably unreachable in the C; tests assert neither implementation ever produces them. As a robustness extra, the suite also passes against the C library rebuilt at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` and with clang, so the `bool*` strict-aliasing cast isn't producing compiler-dependent behavior."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101,"cache_read_input_tokens":186608,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ed4de6b-919a-4d53-801a-50c4e7a84d16","uuid":"9dc414ba-2e9f-455c-8e36-15a742561df8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T18:23:49.176Z"}
